    "practice": "Representing",
    "why": "The student must interpret the visual design of the stained-glass window and translate it into mathematical representations, such as identifying the dimensions of the panels, recognizing geometric shapes (rectangles, semicircles, quarter circles), and determining which parts are clear glass and which are colored glass. This involves creating a mental or written model of the window’s composition to calculate areas and perimeters accurately.",
    "likely_errors": "A student might misidentify the shapes or their positions (e.g., confusing quarter circles with semicircles) or incorrectly assume the entire panel is one shape, leading to wrong area calculations. This is moderately likely, especially if the student does not carefully analyze the image."
