  {
    "order": 2,
    "practice": "Abstracting and Generalizing",
    "why": "The student must generalize the relationship between the original window and the scaled-up version using a scale factor of 3. This includes understanding that area scales by the square of the scale factor (3² = 9) and perimeter by the scale factor (3), and applying this to all materials: glass, joining material, and frame. The student must extend the original cost calculations to the larger window using proportional reasoning.",
