  },
  {
    "order": 3,
    "practice": "Procedural Fluency",
    "why": "After setting up the scaled-up dimensions and areas, the student must perform accurate arithmetic: compute the total area of clear and colored glass, multiply by unit costs, compute the perimeter for the joining material and frame, and sum all costs. This requires fluency in multiplication, addition, and decimal operations with money.",
